    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278k">

                <pb facs="d278k-1" n="1" xml:id="d278k-1"/>

                <head>278K. Letter from CIA Director McCone to Allen
                        W. Dulles, February 19<anchor n="1" xml:id="d278k-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-02-19">February 19, 1962</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Allen:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I have received your memorandum of 15 February 1962 containing your comments on
                    the Inspector General’s Survey of the Cuban Operation. Copies of this
                    memorandum, together with the DD/P analysis of
                    the survey, the comments made by General Cabell, Mr. Kirkpatrick, and the personal views expressed by Mr.
                        Tracy Barnes, will be bound in the
                    report—and therefore will be known to anyone who might have occasion to read
                    it.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_MJA_1">John A.
                            McCone</signed>
                    <affiliation>Director</affiliation>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
